# A long list of siblings (roadmap os-server.md P15, the kernel's review,
# finding 13): an endpoint copied into every slot of twelve spaces of 256;
# six of the spaces deleted - each slot's delete takes one copy out of the
# endpoint's ring of 3,072, at once - then the endpoint, its other 1,536
# copies put in its place in its untyped's ring at once (P15).
# Interrupts are off longest in a space's retype (call 09: its 8 KB zeroed
# at once), never in a delete or a revoke, and never for half a tick
# (before: a delete walked its older siblings, and an adoption all the
# children, in one stretch: 21.7 ms, once the measure could tell, P15).
# tests/programs/additions.asm, TEST_ADD_SIBLINGS; on Bochs, whose timing
# the measure needs.
program: additions
define: TEST_CAPS
define: TEST_ADD_SIBLINGS
define: TEST_STRETCH
emulators: bochs
match: contains
timeout: 180
---
additions: copies made (3072): 3072
additions: half the spaces deleted with them (0): 0
additions: the endpoint deleted (0): 0
additions: done
rx286: interrupts off at most {...} us, at vector 31, call 09
rx286: interrupts never off for 10 ms
